  "text": "[warm] The front door deserves its own dig, so we step off the core again. Seven captures, seven real commits — and every one still opens straight from the blob;  the plaque shows the one-line git command. [short pause] It was born a grid of cards that re-tiled at every ship.\n\n\nFive days in, someone drew it by hand. The source admits it: no layout engine — hand-placed. Within hours, the map began automating itself.\n\n\nTwo days later it had districts, slots, and a name: The Orrery Estate. [short pause] Then it hit the wall every map hits — density. Two philosophies fought here.\n\n\nThe Loupe: magnify, don't move.\n\n\nThe Fairground Gate: descend. The shipping commit stakes the claim: proving depth not a scorer tweak relieved the crowding.\n\n\n\n\nOne week that gate ran false-green under synthetic clicks. The fix says what it learned: the gate now takes a real pointer click. [short pause] And the Great House — the overcrowded manor rebuilt by the loop, from a bug sown from outside the walls. It never knew who asked.\n\n\n[pause] Seven doors. The same address.  The map that redraws itself is the estate's oldest habit — and its most fought-over ground.",
